WEBVTT

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:03.930
Of the three siblings in
the Sumimura family,

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:07.030
the second son. Yoshimori. Was born
with the Hoin Mark.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.530
Though the Legitimate Heir,
his techniques lack stability,

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.700
but he makes up for it with
an overabundance of power.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:19.940
The eldest son. Masamori.
Does not have the Hoin Mark.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:25.620
He left home years ago and
is now the chief of the Night Troops,

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.640
a group of Specially-Talented people
within the Shadow Organization.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.030
And the third son. Toshimori.
Does not have the Hoin Mark either.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.860
Though he may lack
experience as a Caster,

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:44.500
he displays the calmness and intelligence
that his older brother Yoshimori lacks.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:52.780
The dangerous forest invites me
It's showtime again tonight

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.650
(Ayakashi NIGHT)

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:59.850
Everyone's rampaging
with all their strength

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.750
(Fighting late into the night)

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:05.190
Drive away all hesitation

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:09.600
Wanna take them on? Yeah

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.130
I will protect you
(No matter what)

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:16.470
I will protect you that's all
(that's all I want)

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:22.140
Goodbye to the days
when all I'd do was cry

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.640
Sha la la la la...

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:33.050
I hold words in my heart
that I'd like to say

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:35.020
(Secret romance)

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:40.230
Standing in front of me is someone
I don't want to lose

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.990
(A strange distance)

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:48.840
I can't stand watching
people get hurt anymore

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:49.900
Yeah

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:53.370
I wanna be your knight
(I wanna be strong)

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:56.980
I wanna be your light
(More than I am now)

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:02.310
Someday I'll share with you
my 100% smile

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.200
Toshimori, I'm counting on you
to look after the house.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.130
Okay.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:32.710
I don't feel right leaving
the house for a day, but

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:35.880
it's the senior citizen
community hiking trip!

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:39.050
All the senior citizens in
the neighborhood... assemble!

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.650
Going out so early in the morning?

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:49.460
As expected, the "ancillary"
family sure is carefree.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.460
You... Did you forget about it?

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:56.130
All the senior citizens in
the neighborhood are meeting up!

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:58.940
What an elderly thing to do!
How boring!

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:00.260
You've said it now!

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.170
You must be uncomfortable
all wet like that!

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:08.580
This is the Yukimura-style
Natural Clothes Dryer.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:11.480
Those two sure are energetic.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.410
You have a meeting with your editor
about your novel, right?

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:18.220
Yeah. Yoshimori is still sleeping,
so please take care of him.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.420
I just have to wake him up,

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:21.690
so he won't be late to school?

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:25.160
It's hard to tell which one of you
is the older brother.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:28.700
It's okay. I always look after him.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.230
All right. I'm off.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:31.430
Bye!

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:36.130
Father, you should also get going
or you'll be late.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.610
That's right!

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.840
I can't be messing around with the neighbor
who has too much time on their hands!

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:41.870
Now if you'll...

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:43.840
What are you doing?!

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:47.280
You're going to be late!
I'm going ahead!

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:50.690
Wait! You said you weren't going!

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:54.530
I said it was boring.
I didn't say I wasn't going!

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.630
- You're splitting hairs!
- It's so peaceful.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:05.100
As the Legitimate Heir Yoshi seems
to be working hard at a lot of things.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:08.700
But as an older brother

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:09.800
he's not dependable.

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:24.350
Well, I'm going ahead because I'll be late.

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:25.690
Yeah.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.590
Why is he in such a rush?

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:35.630
Tosho!

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:39.430
Morning!

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:40.370
Hey!

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:43.470
Morning?
We'll be late if we don't hurry.

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:47.680
It's totally fine!

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:50.250
Oh yeah...
Did you do your homework?

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.420
Of course... I didn't.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:54.490
It'll be okay!

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:59.530
I really don't think it'll be okay.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.220
You kids!

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.930
I told you to do it and
you didn't do it again?!

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:07.900
Yes...

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:15.440
Fine... I understand that kids
your age want to play.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:19.570
That's right. I have to hang out with friends,
play games and watch anime.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:20.810
I'm just so busy.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:25.110
If you finish this by tomorrow,
I'll forgive you!

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:27.120
It's a special assignment!

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:30.690
I told you so.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:36.360
Tosho.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:38.260
Hey.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:39.990
You're not doing anything
later today, right?

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:42.360
I have some work for
the library committee.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:44.660
But you're free after that, right?

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:51.680
You want me to help you with
your special assignment?

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:53.470
Right on, Tosho!

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:54.950
You know everything!

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.380
I can't. You have to do it yourself.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:00.410
What's the point of the teacher
giving the assignment to you?

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:03.960
I don't want to be lectured
by someone our age!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.860
Are you really nine?

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:09.030
I keep telling you.

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:11.200
Even if your answers are wrong

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:13.030
if you do your homework,

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:16.630
the teacher won't punish you
with assignments like this.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:21.040
Tosho. No human is made
perfectly like that...

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:24.680
Come on! Help us!

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:29.880
But... what's in it for me?

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:33.780
Whoa! He looks so cute. But
he says things only a devil would say...

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.720
Do you understand the word, friendship?

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:39.990
Sometimes, being a good friend
means not helping.

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:45.230
We'll do the problems ourselves,
just give us some pointers on how to do them.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:46.900
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.430
We'll understand better

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:53.460
and the one doing the teaching
can learn too.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.670
Plus, our friendship will be maintained
and everyone will be happy.

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:58.200
That's a great idea, Konta!

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:01.710
In the long run, doesn't that
still work more to your advantage?

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:04.850
Come on! Please!

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:12.120
Other smart guys have cram school.
You're our only hope!

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.760
We'll wait until you're done with
your work at the library.

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:15.860
Come on. Please?

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.260
Oh. Fine.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:21.960
Awesome!

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.100
Wait, we're going to my house?

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:28.810
Yeah. It's okay, right?

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:31.870
We should go to Konta's place
like we usually do.

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:33.510
Your parents aren't home
during the day, right?

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:37.140
For the first time in a while, my dad
took the day off, so he's sleeping.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:38.410
What about your place, Gatcho?

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:41.950
It's cramped and
my other brothers are too noisy.

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:44.750
We've never been to
your house, Tosho.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:47.030
You have to show us
your dog, Masurao

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:48.150
or whatever his name was.

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:51.160
Madarao doesn't like strangers.

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:54.190
It's all right. He'll like us
once we play with him!

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.430
Yeah.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:58.190
Dad and Grandpa are out too...

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:00.930
These two will definitely
make a mess in the house.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:07.340
So, why not?

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:10.340
You know...

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:17.620
My older brother is really scary.
Can you behave yourself?

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.890
S-Scary?

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:22.420
What is your brother like?

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:26.330
I'm surprised that I'm still alive.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:29.460
He trains at home to
make himself stronger.

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:34.540
And at night,
he runs around town...

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:37.440
If he sees anyone he doesn't like...

00:08:37.880 --> 00:08:39.010
He erases them.

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:45.110
Can you stay quiet?

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:46.580
Yes.

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:50.850
I guess this should be okay.
It's not like I lied.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:52.680
What...

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:54.590
kind of older brother is he?

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:14.410
I've never been to this area.

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:16.910
There's nothing but big houses here.

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:19.550
You think Tosho is rich?

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:24.280
Tokine!

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.590
Toshimori-kun.
Are you on your way home?

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:29.290
Yup!

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:31.760
Tosho, is that your sister?

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:32.530
No.

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:33.360
Your friends?

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:34.060
Yup.

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:39.400
Are you eating on the run?

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:43.970
You know it's bad manners.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:47.740
Okay...

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:52.980
Oh. Toshimori-kun.

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:56.320
Do you think Yoshimori has
been acting strange recently?

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:57.620
Really?

00:09:58.590 --> 00:10:00.890
After he went to fix Lord Uro's bed.

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:05.560
Actually he's been acting strange
since Masamori-san visited...

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:08.230
Yoshi is always strange though...

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:12.130
I guess you wouldn't really understand.

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:14.440
I'm sorry. Don't worry about it.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:19.210
Bye!

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:21.380
Bye-bye!

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:29.920
That's great! And she lives
in a mansion. Too.

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:31.650
She's a rich girl, huh?

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:33.080
Hey, Tosho?

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:35.560
What are you doing? Hurry up.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:37.020
Huh?

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:38.900
This is where you live?!

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:39.760
Yeah.

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:43.130
Whoa! Awesome!

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:46.110
Masurao's not here! Masurao! Masurao!

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:48.570
Madarao goes out during the day.

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:49.670
Hey!

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:51.270
There's a storehouse!

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:53.010
Let's go look for treasures!

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:53.810
Hey.

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:57.980
You better behave yourself or
my scary brother will come after you!

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:07.990
Listen. My brother is really scary.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:10.990
Fine. We'll be quiet. Right?

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:11.990
Yeah.

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:18.930
Hey, Toshimori. Welcome back.

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:25.910
You having friends over? Welcome.

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:30.880
Hey Toshimori. I don't see
Grandpa Shige or Dad around.

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:34.820
Grandpa went on a hiking trip
with the seniors

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:37.950
and Dad is in Tokyo meeting
with his editor.

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:39.390
They won't be back until later.

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:41.150
Oh, really?

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:43.220
I already told you!

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:45.730
That's the scary brother?

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:49.700
Then what are we going
to do for dinner?

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:53.070
Dad should have left a note
in the cupboard.

00:11:56.440 --> 00:12:01.400
Anyway, Yoshi, we're going to go study,
so don't bother us!

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:02.240
Okay.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:03.680
- Sorry to intrude.
- Hello.

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:13.390
Hey! Your brother wasn't scary at all!

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:15.490
I think he's a lot like us!

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:18.060
Why does he dress like a mom?

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:19.820
You ruined it Yoshi!

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:22.600
And, your dad is a novelist?

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:25.100
Never mind that!
Let's do the assignment!

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:30.670
Toshimori looked kind of mad.

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:32.700
That reminds me...

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:35.310
He said there's a note
in the cupboard.

00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:37.210
Here it is.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:41.910
"Grandpa won't be home today either,"

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:45.410
"so I asked Mrs. Yukimura
to fix you dinner."

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:49.000
"Tokine might bring it over."

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:50.090
"Just maybe!"

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.060
Tokine is going to bring it over?!

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:56.000
Tokine's dinner delivery...

00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:06.070
Thanks for waiting!

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:10.110
All right!

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:18.720
So over here...

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:20.430
You have to multiply using
the first digit.

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:21.830
You guys!

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:24.620
What's that? Is that your brother?

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:27.590
Snack delivery!

00:13:35.110 --> 00:13:37.740
Awesome! Did you make
this yourself?!

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:38.440
Yeah!

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:41.840
Can we eat it all?! Can we?!

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:43.580
Eat as much as you want!

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:45.950
Why is he in such a good mood?

00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:47.520
All right!

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:49.080
Let's eat!

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:52.450
This is yummy!

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:56.750
Really? You always need something
sweet after using your brain.

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:58.160
Eat up!

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:00.390
Wait a minute Yoshi.
We have to study.

00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:02.530
Don't worry about it! Eat up!

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:03.870
That's not what I meant...

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:14.170
I can't eat anymore!

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:15.710
Eating my fill of cake...

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:18.270
is happiness!

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:21.150
Honestly Yoshi
you ruined everything...

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:24.520
I wonder
why he's the Legitimate Heir.

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:29.290
Can I bring home some leftovers
to my younger brothers?

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:31.690
Look, we're not making any progress.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:34.860
Lucky. I wish I had a brother
that made stuff like this for me...

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:37.260
Plus, your house is so huge.

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:40.800
Yeah. I've never seen
a house as big as this.

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:42.200
I know!

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:47.610
Let's go exploring!

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:48.670
What?

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:50.480
Sounds like an idea! I'm in!

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:51.740
Hey!

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.890
Come on! Your parents
aren't home right?

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:56.050
No!

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:58.790
This place is huge!
How many rooms do you have?

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.730
Wow, you even have a pond!

00:15:05.270 --> 00:15:07.030
Is this wall scroll a treasure?

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:09.100
Why don't you send it in to
that TV show to get it appraised?

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.570
This house is full of sliding doors!

00:15:12.270 --> 00:15:13.210
Hey!

00:15:15.610 --> 00:15:17.100
Do you have any secret rooms?!

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:19.110
Woof woof! Masurao!
Where are you?!

00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:21.210
I want to go see the storehouse.

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:22.870
Let's go treasure hunting!

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:24.750
Woof woof! Beware of dog!

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:27.820
Come out here. Masurao!
Let's play together!

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:29.580
S-Stop!

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:33.220
Let's go over there next!

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:36.660
I said stop it!

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:44.530
Yoshi...

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:51.300
What should I do?

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:08.320
It looked like they were going
to wreck the house

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:10.630
so I used a Kekkai
without realizing it...

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:12.720
And then...

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:17.060
Stop it!

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:35.050
They bumped into
my Kekkai really hard...

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:38.990
I moved them here.
But they're not waking up.

00:16:42.630 --> 00:16:46.330
If they don't wake up,
it'll be my fault...

00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:49.340
It's because I'm inexperienced
and used a Kekkai.

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:53.270
Don't worry about it.

00:16:54.170 --> 00:16:55.770
They're just dizzy.

00:16:56.710 --> 00:16:58.770
They'll wake up in a bit.

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:02.210
But... I used a Kekkai
on my friends.

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:07.220
I always use Kekkai to trip
my friends.

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:10.110
Tokine does that to me all the time.

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:15.950
But I think you should practice
using the techniques a little more.

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:24.260
You know... Tokine said you've changed recently.

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:25.400
Tokine did?

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:26.400
Yeah.

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:28.540
Oh...

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:31.970
I don't really understand it all,

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:35.780
but I've had a lot of things
on my mind recently...

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:40.810
Tokine!

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:42.120
Yes?

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:45.550
Can you deliver this next door?

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:46.850
Sure.

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:52.630
Shuji-san and Grandpa Shigemori
aren't home today.

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:54.000
Oh, really?

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:57.630
Can you heat it up over there
and put it on plates?

00:17:57.940 --> 00:17:58.600
Sure.

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:02.270
Hello?

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:06.070
Yoshimori.

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:08.840
Is he not home?

00:18:10.350 --> 00:18:11.910
Oh, it's open.

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:13.650
I'm coming in.

00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:15.890
Yoshimori, are you there?

00:18:17.060 --> 00:18:18.350
How careless!

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:20.660
Hey, Yoshimori!

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:25.960
They're awake.

00:18:26.570 --> 00:18:28.130
Hey? Where's Masurao?

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:31.300
Um... Why was I sleeping?

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:32.730
I'm... sorry...

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:34.470
You should keep icing your head for now.

00:18:35.310 --> 00:18:38.680
According to Toshimori,
you two fell pretty hard.

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:40.010
Right?!

00:18:41.980 --> 00:18:43.210
Did we fall?

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:45.010
I don't remember.

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:47.050
Does it hurt anywhere else?

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:50.110
Tokine?!

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:55.530
What happened, Tokine?!

00:18:58.100 --> 00:18:59.460
Don't come near me!

00:18:59.770 --> 00:19:01.930
What? I can't?

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:05.530
Get away! Get away!

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:08.330
Nooo!

00:19:19.390 --> 00:19:23.410
In times like this I wish I could have used
the Kekkai techniques better.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:25.620
But I wasn't used to it.

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:30.960
I was expecting a technique from
the Legitimate Heir...

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:36.030
But Yoshi was more
preoccupied with Tokine.

00:19:57.160 --> 00:19:59.630
Y-Yoshi... mori.

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:10.170
Yoshimori?!
Are you all right, Yoshimori?!

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:16.570
Hot! Hot!

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:20.940
I still smell like curry.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:23.480
I'm sorry about everything today.

00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:25.510
Don't worry about it.

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:27.010
But in exchange...

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:32.050
Can you tell us the answers
to the assignment?

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:34.720
Friendship is such a good thing!

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:39.560
I tried but could not help
my friends in the long run.

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:47.600
I'm s-sorry... I just can't stand those...
black things.

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:52.110
I should have used a Kekkai.
I'm sorry.

00:20:57.450 --> 00:21:00.080
I'm sorry about all the ruckus today.

00:21:00.490 --> 00:21:05.790
It was pretty fun.
Your brother was weird but fun!

00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:07.760
But I wanted to see Masurao.

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:12.590
My oldest brother is
a lot more calm and cool.

00:21:12.630 --> 00:21:14.970
Huh? But he's a good brother!

00:21:15.070 --> 00:21:16.330
He can make sweets. Too!

00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:19.460
Hm... Well, I guess...

00:21:21.610 --> 00:21:22.840
Bye-bye!

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.610
Tosho! See you tomorrow!

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:26.200
Yeah!

00:21:27.380 --> 00:21:31.750
Well Yoshi. I guess
it turned out all right.

00:21:37.590 --> 00:21:40.080
For dinner we ended up
ordering delivery.

00:21:42.430 --> 00:21:44.160
Delivery. After all that...

00:21:44.560 --> 00:21:47.260
I wanted to eat Tokine's curry.

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:54.300
Tokine didn't make the curry
but Yoshi was still depressed.

00:21:57.140 --> 00:21:59.840
Hey! Isn't this pork cutlet bowl delicious?!

00:22:00.510 --> 00:22:04.350
Yoshi is really simple-minded
so he recovered right away.

00:22:15.400 --> 00:22:19.460
Yoshi is still in training
to be the Legitimate Heir.

00:22:20.570 --> 00:22:26.700
But as an older brother...
it looks like he can be reliable sometimes.

00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:52.390
I will take the road
I believe in anywhere

00:22:53.030 --> 00:22:56.800
Wanting to protect what's
in front of my eyes

00:22:57.500 --> 00:23:01.100
The world I have yet
to know is endless

00:23:01.910 --> 00:23:05.540
I know it will make
my heart dance

00:23:07.350 --> 00:23:18.020
I feel like I could fly
for the one I love

00:23:18.060 --> 00:23:26.760
Even if I search the whole world
no one could replace you

00:23:27.470 --> 00:23:31.600
Not everyone has a tomorrow

00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:40.210
Don't cry

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:48.950
Even if I search the whole world
no one could replace you

00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:53.790
We weren't born
to hurt each other

00:23:53.830 --> 00:24:02.200
Don't cry
